WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.190
Win partners, build an honest agent network, and plan 90 days of growth.

2
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:11.490
This is the video for module 3: Winning Partners, Building an Agent Network and Planning Growth.

3
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:20.920
A shop owner's real question is not, is this product nice? It is, will it sell from my shelf and make me money without trouble?

4
00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:30.340
So your pitch answers with facts. Your one-page sell sheet shows the price, the trade price, and the shop's margin per unit in naira.

5
00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:37.900
It also shows your minimum order, delivery time, payment terms, and proof that the product already sells.

6
00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:46.400
Step one. List 10 to 15 outlets whose customers match yours: pharmacies, salons, gyms, mini-marts.

7
00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:54.570
Step two. Visit first as a shopper. Note similar products, their prices, and who decides what is stocked.

8
00:00:55.820 --> 00:01:02.050
Step three. Ask the decision maker for a short meeting at a quiet hour, not on a busy Saturday.

9
00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:13.190
Step four. Let them try the sample, tell them what they earn per unit, and offer a small trial, for example 12 units, reviewed after 4 to 6 weeks.

10
00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:23.750
Step five. Follow up the same day. And put the trial in writing. A no today is often a not yet, so return politely on the date they give you.

11
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:40.530
For example, Amaka sells shea body butter. She got trial orders at a pharmacy and a gym. Sell-through is the share of delivered stock that sells. The pharmacy sold 9 of 12 jars, which is 75%, and reordered.

12
00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:57.710
The gym sold only 3, which is 25%. Members did not see the jars, and staff could not answer questions. So she offers a shelf sign and a 15-minute staff briefing. If sales stay low, she collects her stock and moves on.

13
00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:08.580
Agents carry your product into places you never visit, and they carry your reputation too. Look for a hairdresser, a fitness coach, a women's group leader.

14
00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:15.340
Ask for a referee, take a copy of a valid ID, and record their phone number and area.

15
00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:21.370
Start with three to five agents you can train well, not twenty you cannot follow up.

16
00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:31.600
Keep the same terms for every agent at the same level, for example 10% commission, rising to 12% above 50 units a month.

17
00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:44.200
Never promise income you cannot prove, and never charge a fee to join. Schemes that earn from recruiting people, not selling products, are a warning sign of a pyramid scheme.

18
00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:56.520
Teach these rules in every training, and have each agent sign the agreement. First, cash: customers pay into your business account, never into an agent's personal account.

19
00:02:57.770 --> 00:03:03.490
Second, stock: limit what a new agent holds until trust is built, and record every unit.

20
00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:08.640
Third, data: customer phone numbers and addresses stay private.

21
00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:15.120
In October her agents sold 40, 25, 12, 8 and 0 jars.

22
00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:20.740
That is 85 jars, or 340,000 naira of sales.

23
00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:24.760
She pays 34,000 naira in commission.

24
00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:33.820
Ifeoma, her best agent, earns 16,000 naira. Amaka asks her to share her approach on the next agent call.

25
00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:44.200
Ruth has sold nothing for two months, so she is offered a refresher or a friendly exit. And customers asking for a smaller size becomes a product idea.

26
00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:56.800
Now plan one new channel for 90 days. In days 1 to 15, fix your gaps. Amaka adds a production day and sets aside 200,000 naira of working cash.

27
00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:01.670
In days 16 to 30, build your sell sheet and target list.

28
00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:08.730
In days 31 to 60, pitch and run trials, with a first shelf check after 2 weeks.

29
00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:14.540
In days 61 to 90, measure sell-through, payments and true profit.

30
00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:22.740
Write number targets before you start, like at least 3 outlets reordering. Grow in pharmacies cannot be judged at day 90.

31
00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:29.750
To remember. Pitch with facts and a small written trial, and judge it by sell-through and reorders.

32
00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:34.950
Keep agents honest with clear terms, and money going only to your business account.

33
00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:42.980
At day 90, expand, adjust or exit using your targets. One channel done well beats three opened at once.

34
00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:51.010
Now prepare your pitch kit, design your agent programme, and draft your capstone portfolio and 90-day plan.

35
00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:53.300
Continue with the lessons below.
